question:
What is the compiler result of the following Java snippet?
```java
byte a = 10;
byte b = 20;
byte c = a + b;
System.out.println(c);
```

What is printed by the following code snippet?
```java
byte b = 127;
b++;
System.out.println(b);
```

What is the result of compiling and executing the following snippet?
```java
float f = 3.14;
System.out.println(f);
```

What is the output of evaluating `a == b` and `c == d` in the following code?
```java
Integer a = 127;
Integer b = 127;
Integer c = 128;
Integer d = 128;
System.out.println((a == b) + " " + (c == d));
```

What happens when compiling the following code snippet?
```java
byte b = 5;
b += 10;
b = b + 10;
```

What does the following snippet print?
```java
char c = 'A';
System.out.println(c + 1);
```

What is the output of the following Java snippet?
```java
int x = 10;
if (false && ++x > 0) {
    // do nothing
}
System.out.println(x);
```

What happens when you compile the following method?
```java
public void testScope() {
    int a;
    if (true) {
        a = 5;
    }
    System.out.println(a);
}
```

What is the result of attempting to compile this method in Java?
```java
public void checkShadowing() {
    int x = 100;
    {
        int x = 200;
        System.out.println(x);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following ternary expression?
```java
Object result = true ? 10 : 20.0;
System.out.println(result.getClass().getName() + " " + result);
```

What happens when executing the following snippet?
```java
final int[] numbers = {1, 2, 3};
numbers[0] = 99;
System.out.println(numbers[0]);
```

What is the result of casting a double with value `128.9` to `byte`?
```java
double d = 128.9;
byte b = (byte) d;
System.out.println(b);
```
